    {
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## MAXXAM AI — LinkedIn Poster\n\n**Flow:** Schedule → read Content_Calendar → filter → post → write result back.\n\nPublishes a row when **all three** are true:\n`status = approved` · `platform = LinkedIn` · `schedule_date = today`\n\nRows with a non-empty `image_url` take the image branch; everything else posts as text.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Point both Google Sheets nodes at your Content Calendar\n2. Connect a LinkedIn OAuth2 credential (Share on LinkedIn product, `w_member_social`)\n3. Set `person` on both LinkedIn nodes to your `urn:li:person:XXXX`\n4. Set Workflow Settings → Timezone BEFORE trusting the cron",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Gotchas",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Hard-won gotchas — read before editing\n\n1. **Column is `schedule_date`, not `scheduled_date`.** The filter silently matches nothing if this is wrong.\n2. **Merge must be `append`, not `combine`.** Only one branch ever fires; `combine` waits for both, yields nothing, and the write-back never runs — so the row stays `approved` and reposts every day.\n3. **The LinkedIn node returns `urn`, not `id`.** Build the post URL from `$json.urn`.\n4. **Download Image is a Google Drive node, not HTTP.** A plain HTTP node returns parsed text, not binary. Public `uc?export=download` links return a sign-in page. Use `/file/d/<ID>/view` with an authenticated Drive credential.\n5. **`image_url` routes on non-empty, not on validity.** A placeholder like `GRAPHIC_NEEDED` sends the row down the image branch and fails it. Real link or empty.\n6. **Error outputs are wired.** Both LinkedIn nodes use `onError: continueErrorOutput` into Mark Failed. n8n still reports the execution as SUCCESS when an error is caught — judge outcomes by the sheet's `status`, not the execution list.\n7. **Set the workflow timezone.** Without it the server default applies and `0 8 * * 1-5` is not your 8am.\n8. **LinkedIn tokens expire every 60 days with no refresh** outside the partner programme. Reconnect via Credentials → Switch account.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 3
      }
    }
